Subject: [PATCH 01360/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for
 VERIFIER-AS-ONLINE-ACTION-PRUNER efficiency (the north-star 'efficient' axis;
 RE-RUN of the .375 exp4061 that was poison-test-cascade-SKIPPED; the pivot
 from the banked G2 WM-planning negative): the GAP-4 verifier is proven CHEAP
 (95.3x cheaper than an LLM-judge at parity, .371 exp4026) and accurate; this
 measures it as an ONLINE action-pruner in the live ARC harness. On 3-5 of the
 SOLVED games, run the explore-first solver WITH vs WITHOUT the GAP-4 verifier
 pruning candidate actions before execution (prune actions the verifier
 predicts are inconsistent with the induced mechanic / will not advance the
 goal predicate). Measure actions-to-solve + wall-clock at EQUAL solve-rate
 (the pruner MUST NOT reduce solve-rate -- positive control). Per
 arXiv:2603.10282 (update-free on-policy steering via verifiers) +
 arXiv:2602.01070 (online verification beats post-hoc reranking). Honest null
 (no efficiency gain) is a COMPLETE verdict.

